/-!
# The marked nonsplit Aut(M₁₂) model and its compatible transport

The actual first core has its original quaternion embeddings and marked Z.
Its literal other preimage is C₄ × E₄, with z corresponding to (2,0). Squaring
induces a nonzero homomorphism A/Z → Z with kernel of order four. An explicit
first-parabolic cubic acts as the prescribed cubic on the actual wreath quotient.

The whole-overlap marked pair, all previous obstruction results, and the
original split movement model remain exported. Transport uses the recognized
full amalgam isomorphism, including both inclusion squares, and gives the
order-24 first-parabolic quotient when the actual other preimage is normal.
These concrete model facts do not assert the larger-ambient rigidity theorem.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith 14.2.21, printed p.988 / PDF p.1005,
refs/quasithin.pdf, with the corrected nonsplit third-core calculation.
-/
